      "Memory: only the 30-minute nap improved recognition performance (A′) versus staying awake; 10 and 60 minutes did not reach significance vs wake.",
      "Sleep inertia: immediate post-wake slowing was seen after 30- and 60-minute naps (especially on processing-speed reaction time), but this resolved within ~30 minutes."
