    summary: "This review explains the two-way relationship between REM sleep and body temperature control. During REM sleep, normal thermoregulation is largely suspended, making the body temporarily less able to respond to heat or cold. At the same time, strong activation of heat-producing systems, such as during cold exposure, reduces the likelihood of entering REM sleep.",
