    summary: "Researchers surveyed 10,106 adults in Saudi Arabia about which devices were in their bedroom, how often they used them at bedtime, and how they slept. Having multiple devices nearby mattered less than actually using them while in bed. Frequent bedtime use of smartphones, computers, and other devices was tied to worse sleep quality, longer time to fall asleep (especially phones and tablets), and a higher risk of excessive daytime sleepiness.",
