    title: "Forgetting is Interference",
    excerpt: "People confused similar memories more when they had stored more similar items, suggesting interference matters more than time for losing fine details.",
    date: "2022.07.18",
    readTime: "35 min",
    journal: "Frontiers in Behavioral Neuroscience",
