    summary: "Across two studies, researchers tested whether daily changes in arousal influence sustained attention. Although sleepiness followed a clear inverted-u pattern across the day, sustained attention performance remained largely stable. Both within-person and between-person analyses showed little to no relationship between subjective sleepiness and attention accuracy or speed.",
