    impact: "If your goal is fewer heart problems over time, reducing saturated fat and replacing it with unsaturated fats may help, especially for lowering overall cardiovascular events. But you should not expect this change alone to clearly reduce your chance of dying, based on current evidence. In real life, it works best as part of a full heart-healthy pattern, like replacing butter and fatty processed meats with foods like olive oil, nuts, seeds, fish, and high-fiber meals.",
    constraints: "This is an umbrella review, so it depends on the quality of the reviews it included. Many cohort meta-analyses were rated low or critically low quality, and many outcomes were not graded with GRADE. Trial follow-up was often under 10 years, which may be too short to detect differences in mortality.",
