    summary: "This review pulled together research on how breathing rate connects to sports performance from both the body side and the mind side. The authors separate breathing into slow voluntary breathing (about 4-10 breaths per minute) and fast voluntary breathing (over 20 breaths per minute), and argue they can affect performance in different ways. Overall, they suggest slow breathing is more consistently linked to better calm, focus, and recovery, while fast breathing can be useful during hard effort but may also trigger symptoms like anxiety or dizziness if used improperly.",
