    institutions: ["Radboud University Medical Center, Nijmegen, The Netherlands"],
    summary: "Researchers looked at cognitive test results in 1,375 ME/CFS patients and compared them with fatigue and pain levels from questionnaires and 12-day diaries. Fatigue was the most consistent factor linked to worse performance, while pain and physical functioning also mattered for several speed-based tasks. The pain-related link to worse performance was stronger in older patients.",
