    summary: "This paper reviews research on breathing pace in sports, looking at both the body and the mind. Slow, controlled breathing is linked with lower stress, better heart control, and improved focus, which may help performance in some situations. Fast breathing is normal during hard exercise, but outside training it can trigger anxiety-like symptoms, and the review says the best \"ideal\" breathing strategy still is not fully proven.",
