    impact: "For everyday curiosity or low-stakes trending, these trackers may be \"good enough\" when they give a value. But for real postoperative or critical monitoring, the missing readings are the dealbreaker, because a device that often fails can miss early hypoxia when it matters most.",
    constraints: "Most oxygen values were in the 90\u2013100% range, with very few true low-oxygen cases, so the study cannot prove how well these trackers work during significant hypoxia. Also, measurement timing windows differed by device, and only a few repeated readings per patient limited conclusions about repeatability.",
