    summary: "Researchers tested how well older adults' bodies handle the quick change from lying down to standing up. People who showed calmer, more stable responses in blood pressure, breathing, heart rhythm patterns, and balance tended to have better physical function. Some signals linked more to walking speed in women, while certain balance and blood pressure signals linked more to mortality risk in men.",
