    summary: "The study tested how information from different senses can be linked using time-based patterns instead of static snapshots. A collaborative neural network model learned which signals belonged together by noticing when they repeatedly happened at the same time. When signals did not line up in time, the model struggled, similar to how human perception weakens when senses fall out of sync.",
