    summary: "This review analyzed decades of research and found strong, consistent evidence that poor mental health, especially depression and anxiety, reduces workplace productivity. Workers with mental health challenges are more likely to miss work and to work at reduced capacity when present. However, most studies relied on simple survey data, limiting how confidently cause and effect can be determined.",
