    title: "Adolescent Risk and Mind Control",
    excerpt: "Researchers discovered that while strong brain control helps teens avoid danger, a specific type called effortful control also encourages them to take healthy, positive risks.",
    date: "2025.11.24",
    readTime: "12 min",
    journal: "Journal of Research on Adolescence",
