    summary: "University students kept daily diaries for a full semester, showing that good study habits one day\u2014like focusing well, putting in effort, and avoiding delay\u2014make you feel more satisfied with your work that evening. This satisfaction then boosts your interest in studying the next morning while reducing pressure-driven motivation. Planning ahead did not show the same link, but most other habits did, with some patterns differing between busy lecture weeks and quieter exam or break periods.",
