    summary: "The study examined how uneven performance across different thinking skills, called dispersion, changes with age. Adults in their 60s showed a unique pattern, often performing like younger adults on some tasks while resembling much older adults on others. This suggests that some older adults use compensatory strategies, supported by education and cognitive reserve, to maintain performance.",
