    summary: "Life expectancy has jumped by about 26 years since 1950, but healthy years have not kept pace, leaving a roughly 9-year gap filled with disease and frailty. Chronic conditions like heart disease, cancer, diabetes, and lung issues drive most disability in older adults, worsened by frailty that makes people vulnerable to falls and hospitalization. The authors call for combined public health efforts, better medical care, and emerging regenerative treatments to shrink this gap and promote longer, healthier lives for everyone.",
