    summary: "Researchers used wearable sensors to measure real-world walking in 200 adults aged 65 to 94 over one week. They found clear age and sex differences in daily steps, walking speed, stride length, and walking patterns, with mobility declining faster at certain age ranges rather than steadily. The study provides real-life walking benchmarks that can help detect early mobility decline.",
