    summary: "This review shows how past exposure to deadly infections drove changes in human genes that helped people survive diseases like malaria, HIV, and cholera. Some of those same gene versions that protected against infections long ago can now raise risks for other health problems in today's cleaner, less active world with different diets. Combining genetic knowledge with healthy habits like exercise and good nutrition can help reduce vulnerability to infections.",
