    constraints: "Most studies relied on self-reported activity levels rather than objective measurements, which can be inaccurate due to memory errors or overestimation. The review found high variation between studies in how they measured and categorized activity, making direct comparisons challenging. Most participants were from Europe and North America, limiting how well findings apply to other populations. Additionally, the studies could not account for activity changes during the years between measurements and death, and few studies properly adjusted for health factors that change over time and might influence both activity levels and mortality risk.",
