    summary: "Researchers showed people realistic photos of living rooms that were identical except for one thing: the furniture and edges were either curved or angular. Overall, curved rooms were rated as more calming and less stressful, and they were also rated a bit more beautiful and likable. The stress benefits showed up no matter the style, while the beauty and liking boost mainly appeared in modern rooms and was strongest in participants who reported female sex.",
