    constraints: "This study measured self-reported feelings while looking at static images, not real rooms, and it did not directly measure physical stress signals like heart rate or cortisol. The results may also depend on the specific room designs used and on who participated (online sample). The sex categories were limited to male/female as reported in the study, so it cannot explain how gender identity or culture might change these effects.",
