    constraints: "The study was cross-sectional, so it cannot prove cause and effect. Hair quality and length were measured with single self-report items, and all couples were heterosexual and from South Korea, which limits generalization. The effects were statistically small, meaning hair is only one minor factor among many that influence sexual frequency.",
