    impact: "Skin glow does not just change how a face looks, it also changes how the brain responds. Radiant skin appears to trigger stronger reward-related activity, which may explain why glowing skin is often linked to beauty and health. This suggests that subtle changes in skin finish, including through skincare or makeup, can shape social impressions.",
    constraints: "The study included only Japanese women as both participants and face models, so results may not apply to all cultures or genders. Skin reflection was partly created using cosmetics and image editing, which may not perfectly reflect natural skin. The sample size was relatively small, and individual differences were large.",
