    summary: "Researchers tested how 173 students aged 9-14 responded to the same teacher lesson when shown either a photo of a professionally dressed teacher or a casually dressed teacher. Students who saw the professional outfit rated the teacher as more competent, more organized, and younger. They also expected higher grades, were more willing to do extra homework, and viewed the teacher's personality more positively. The simple change in clothing created major differences in how students perceived the same exact lesson.",
