    impact: "What you wear as a teacher genuinely affects how students learn and engage. Professional business clothing creates a better learning environment by making students more motivated, more trusting of the teacher's abilities, and more open to participating. This matters because small changes in presentation can lead to real differences in classroom outcomes. Schools might want to consider dress guidelines not as strict rules, but as tools that help teachers be more effective. For teachers, dressing professionally is not just about appearance but about setting up conditions where students are more likely to succeed.",
    constraints: "The study relied on students self-reporting their perceptions, which may not always reflect their actual behavior in a real classroom. The sample size was relatively small and limited to one region in Romania, so results might differ in other cultures or age groups. The research only tested one type of professional outfit versus casual wear, so we don't know how other clothing styles would perform. Additionally, the study isolated clothing from other factors like facial expressions, which means real-world effects might be more complex when combined with other aspects of teacher appearance.",
